  "sourceAssessment": {
    "basis": [
      "jinshu:053:s0118–s0123 names 太醫令程據 compounding 巴豆杏子丸 at Jia’s order, for 孫慮 to take to the deposed prince in Xuchang. zizhitongjian:083:s0233–s0240 repeats the same panic, 太醫令程據 preparing poison, 孫慮, Xuchang and subsequent killing with a medicine pestle. Exact full name, medical office and distinctive event establish one poison preparer.",
      "jinshu:053:s0131 lists 劉振、孫慮、程據 executed after Jia’s death; zizhitongjian:083:s0273–s0274 lists 劉振、董猛、孫慮、程據 in the same fall-of-Jia sequence. jinshu:031:s0560 and zizhitongjian:083:s0068 earlier name 太醫令程據 in Jia’s intimate circle; full name, identical specific office and the same court connect these earlier members to that later official."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Read all 120 Chinese units, nine complete blocks, four complete singleton records, 21 owned claims and 12 mentions; both English fields at every owned anchor. No inbound owned relationship claims supplied. No conflicting native place, kinship, sex or polity evidence appears.",
      "All physician/official roles and 太醫令 office claims are compatible. Existing AD291–300 interval, Jin053 AD300 contextual attestations and death claim remain untouched, as do the undated Tongjian claims. No new dates or relationships are inferred.",
      "External Tongjian s0236 English says guimao although Chinese prints 癸未. This English cyclical-day error does not distinguish a second Cheng Ju; it is disclosed and preserved for a separate source workflow, without correcting any date in this identity draft.",
      "One fresh transitive merge covers all four complete canonical members and all three owned pairs. Old evidence is historical context only; no approval rebinding or source/extraction change."
    ]
